arning models widely used for practical inference, deployed in various platforms, and central to the paper's focus on improving model efficiency.", 'A type of deep neural network used for image recognition and other tasks, the focus of this research for improving inference.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'Convolution layers': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['Layers in CNNs that perform the majority of the computation, and are the focus of efforts to improve inference speed through sparsity.', 'Layers within a CNN that perform convolution operations, crucial for feature extraction and a key area for speed optimization through sparsity.', 'Layers in a CNN that apply convolutional filters to the input data.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'SpMV': {'type': ['method', 'method'], 'description': ['Sparse Matrix-Vector multiplication, a fundamental operation in sparse linear algebra, relevant to sparse CNNs as it is used in sparse convolution implementations.', 'Sparse Matrix-Vector multiplication, a fundamental operation in sparse linear algebra, relevant for sparse convolution performance analysis.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'GEMM': {'type': ['method', 'GENERIC', 'method'], 'description': ['General Matrix-Matrix Multiplication, a core operation in dense linear algebra, often used as a baseline for comparison with sparse convolution methods.', 'General Matrix Multiplication, a fundamental operation in fully connected layers.', 'General Matrix Multiplication, a core operation used in fully connected layers and relevant for understanding the computational bottlenecks in CNNs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 1]}, 'SGEMM': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'GENERIC'], 'description': ['Single-precision General Matrix-Matrix Multiplication, a specific implementation of GEMM, often used in the context of CNNs due to the prevalence of single-precision floating-point arithmetic.', 'Sparse General Matrix Multiplication, a variant of GEMM optimized for sparse matrices, relevant to the implementation of fully connected layers.', 'A highly optimized BLAS routine used as a proxy for dense convolution performance.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'DATA TRANSFERS': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The movement of data between different parts of a computer system, such as between memory and the processor, which can introduce overhead in sparse CNNs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Sparse Convolution Overhead': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The additional computational cost and data transfer overhead associated with sparse convolution, particularly the transformation of tensors to matrices.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Small Filters': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The limitation of some sparse convolution methods in their applicability to small filter sizes (e.g., 3x3), which are commonly used in modern CNN architectures.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Dense convolution': {'type': ['GENERIC', 'GENERIC'], 'description': ['Standard convolution operation, used as a baseline for comparison with sparse convolution.', 'Standard convolution operations performed on dense data.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}, 'Direct Sparse Convolution Algorithm': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A specific algorithm introduced in the paper to improve the classification speed of CNNs by directly implementing sparse convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Weight Decay': {'type': ['METHOD'], 'description': ['A regularization technique used to prevent overfitting in machine learning models, particularly in the context of training neural networks. It adds a penalty term to the loss function that discourages large weights.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Regularization Parameters': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['Values used to control the strength of regularization techniques like weight decay. These parameters are tuned to optimize model performance, balancing accuracy and generalization.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'AlexNet': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['A specific CNN architecture used for image classification, used here as a test case.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Speedups': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['Improvements in processing speed, often expressed as a multiple of the original speed.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'CNNs': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Convolutional Neural Networks, a type of deep learning model used for image recognition and other tasks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Server Platform': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The server platform where speedups of convolution layers were demonstrated.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Mobile Platform': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The mobile platform where speedups of convolution layers were demonstrated.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Improve CNN performance': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The overall objective of the research, focusing on enhancing the speed, accuracy, and model size of Convolutional Neural Networks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Classification speed': {'description': ['A critical performance metric for CNNs, targeted for improvement through sparsity techniques, forming part of the "golden trident".', 'The rate at which a model can classify inputs, a key performance metric targeted for improvement.', 'The rate at which a model can classify images, measured in images per second.', 'To improve the classification speed of CNNs.'], 'type': ['task', 'GENERIC'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'ARITHMETIC INTENSITY': {'description': ['A measure of the ratio of computation to data access in a computation, relevant to the efficiency of sparse convolution.'], 'type': ['GENERIC'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}}
